From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb E." <158400752+FoxesRCool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:19:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus: keep the charge limit across
 reboots

qcom_battmgr sets a charge limit through the battery firmware
(charge_control_start_threshold and charge_control_end_threshold), and
the firmware keeps it in PMK8550 SDAM 0x7e00. Without nvmem cells the
driver can't read it back, so sysfs reports 0/0 after every boot
whatever the firmware enforces, and the driver has nothing to send again
when the battery service restarts. Give the pmic-glink node the cells
hamoa-pmics.dtsi already defines, as x1-crd.dtsi and the Acer SFA14-11
do.

On the Surface Laptop 7 13.8" the firmware uses the layout those cells
describe: after setting end=80 through sysfs, SDAM 0x73/0x75/0x76 read
1/80/5, and after start=95 (end 100) they read 1/100/5.

Booted on the 13.8": qcom_battmgr binds and reports 95/100, and the
SDAM bytes are unchanged. The driver doesn't fail safe on a wrong
layout: with a non-zero byte at 0x73 and 0x76 >= 0x75 the
battery driver's probe fails with -EINVAL and the battery and charger
supplies disappear.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
index 2537a10..90477f9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -101,6 +101,13 @@
 		orientation-gpios = <&tlmm 121 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>,
 				    <&tlmm 123 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
+		nvmem-cells = <&charge_limit_en>,
+			      <&charge_limit_end>,
+			      <&charge_limit_delta>;
+		nvmem-cell-names = "charge_limit_en",
+				   "charge_limit_end",
+				   "charge_limit_delta";
+
 		/* Left-side rear port */
 		connector@0 {
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
-- 
